    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement following the codebase's existing side-effect pattern.\n\n**What I added:**\n- `rest/notification/WelcomeNotifier.java` \u2014 a small `@Component` with a single responsibility: enqueuing welcome notifications. It emits via the logger named `NOTIFY` a line containing the owner id and memberId, mirroring the existing `OwnerAuditLogger` (which uses the `AUDIT` logger) so notification side-effects stay out of the request-handling flow.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- Injected `WelcomeNotifier` into `OwnerRestControllerV1` via the constructor (Spring convention) and invoked `welcomeNotifier.welcome(owner)` in the private `createOwner(...)` method, right after the successful save and the existing audit log \u2014 so it fires only on successful create.\n\nI deliberately kept this as its own unit rather than folding it into `OwnerAuditLogger` (which owns audit concerns) or bloating the controller, keeping each class single-responsibility.\n\n**Verification:** The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test), and the acceptance test's captured output confirms the line: `NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
